{"c":[{"id":"1f960dec0850b21e","sum":"Releases stand alone (users skip them); v0.1.0-v2.1.2 pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so wild warehouses are v1.0.0+ at schema 0-8; old-format tests create v1.0.0 on purpose. 1.5.4 opens and replays a v1.0.0+ file a killed 2.0.0 writer left; only v2.0.0+ files are unreadable.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T160004Z-0474312fdfee4cb0","text":"Every stockroom release must stand alone: users skip releases. Releases v0.1.0-v2.1.2 all pinned DuckDB 1.5.4, so warehouses in the wild are v1.0.0+ at schema 1-8. Under DuckDB 2.0, tests that need an old-format file must create it at storage v1.0.0 on purpose.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T161737Z-639a1a68a7083e6a","text":"Measured 2026-10-21: DuckDB 1.5.4 opens (ro and rw) a v1.0.0+ file a crashed DuckDB 2.0.0 writer left with a wal, plain or vss HNSW-indexed, and replays all rows; the wal matches a 1.5.4 writer's in size. Only files 2.0 creates (v2.0.0+) are unreadable before 2.0.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0c27c79ce59ec8d2","sum":"DuckDB 2.0.0: USING COMPRESSION zstd raises BinderException on v1.0.0 storage (1.5.4 ignores it); v1.2.0+ gives ZSTD, so zstd in 0001 breaks v1.0.0 fixtures. 2.0.0 wal replay into an HNSW index breaks it (InternalException or hang); DROP+CREATE+CHECKPOINT repairs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T164029Z-dd6c62dffb711e78","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 raises BinderException for USING COMPRESSION zstd at storage v1.0.0 (1.5.4 stored it uncompressed silently); v1.2.0+ storage gives ZSTD. A zstd clause in 0001 breaks a schema-0 v1.0.0+ file and old-format test fixtures built from current 0001.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T170926Z-f865c4bcdda86174","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 bug: replaying a wal holding inserts into an HNSW-indexed table (killed 1.5.4 or 2.0 writer) breaks the index: query, delete, insert raise InternalException (flat or constant vector) or hang. 1.5.4 replays fine. DROP INDEX, CREATE INDEX, CHECKPOINT repairs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
